From: Eric X. Liu <eric@ericxliu.me>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:06:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] bound_buffers: gate O(N) shape() walk behind 1-second census interval

`bound_buffers::note_registry_levels()` is invoked from the drain thread's
post-tranche sweep (~250-300x/sec). Its own doc comment states that
`BoundBuffers::shape()` is "walked once per census interval", yet
`note_registry_levels()` called `state.bound_buffers.shape()` (allocating a
`HashMap` and iterating every entry, up to 12,000+ entries) BEFORE checking
the 1-second `LAST_MS` gate. This consumed 35-73 ms/sec of drain-thread time
(`post_bindlv_us`) on every active second.

Track `PEAK_ENTRIES` with the existing O(1) `BoundBuffers::len()` method and
only compute `shape()` once per second after winning the `LAST_MS`
compare-exchange.
---
 crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/bound_buffers.rs | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/bound_buffers.rs b/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/bound_buffers.rs
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/bound_buffers.rs
+++ b/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/bound_buffers.rs
@@ -235,10 +235,9 @@ pub fn note_registry_levels(state: &crate::model::DeviceState) {
     static LAST_MS: AtomicU64 = AtomicU64::new(0);
     static PEAK_ENTRIES: AtomicU64 = AtomicU64::new(0);
 
-    let shape = state.bound_buffers.shape();
-    let peak = PEAK_ENTRIES
-        .fetch_max(shape.entries as u64, Ordering::Relaxed)
-        .max(shape.entries as u64);
+    let entries = state.bound_buffers.len() as u64;
+    let peak = PEAK_ENTRIES.fetch_max(entries, Ordering::Relaxed).max(entries);
 
     let now = crate::observe::elapsed_ms() as u64;
     let last = LAST_MS.load(Ordering::Relaxed);
@@ -251,6 +250,7 @@ pub fn note_registry_levels(state: &crate::model::DeviceState) {
     {
         return;
     }
+    let shape = state.bound_buffers.shape();
     crate::observe::off(format!(
         "bound_buffers (levels, not per-interval) entries={} peak={} pairs={} \
          multi_offset_pairs={} max_offsets={}",
-- 
2.47.0
